From bef01acd40e2488a0034f5cf9fa33dab91046924 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akapug <akapug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:09:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] sycl: PTQ1_0 prompt chunks on an XMX copy, decode on
 the row-per-lane mat-vec

#294 rewrites a PTQ1_0 weight in place into its XMX layout on first use, and
from then on every mul_mat on the weight takes XMX. On an Arc Pro B70 with
Ternary Bonsai 2 27B, that wins prompt chunks against the row-per-lane mat-vec
and dequantize path (pp32 543 against 150 tok/s, pp128 975 against 492). It
loses decode (tg64 35.7 against 52.9) and small batches (batched decode at 4
sequences 111 against 149). One layout cannot serve both kernels.

A PTQ1_0 weight now keeps its own layout. The XMX path reads a separate copy
in the 34-byte PQ2_0 XMX layout, in a device allocation of its own that the
weight's extra owns and frees. The first mul_mat with GGML_SYCL_XMX_MIN_ROWS
(default 16) or more columns makes the copy. It reads the weight in whichever
layout the weight has at that time: the loaded blocks, or the layout that the
mat-vec reordered them into. Mul_mats with fewer columns use the weight's own
layout. The buffer no longer reserves room for an in-place expansion.

PQ2_0 keeps #294's in-place path. GGML_SYCL_DISABLE_XMX=1 still keeps both
types off XMX. The copy keeps #294's guards: MUL_MAT only, no views, no split
or COMPUTE buffers, a 2D contiguous weight with a supported ne0, and a 64-byte
aligned XMX weight.

The copies take nelements / 128 * 34 bytes in addition to the weights: 6.02
GiB for the 400 layer weights of Ternary Bonsai 2 27B (4.96 GiB of PTQ1_0).
The output head adds 0.31 GiB when a ubatch has 16 or more outputs. After the
first graph that makes copies, one info line gives their count and size.
